Continuing the dark gunmetal aesthetic of the Mark XIII, Tony designed the Mark XIV with minimal armor plating across the midsection and limbs to drastically cut down weight while maximizing joint articulation. By paring back the heavy defensive shells, he created a suit that could perform razor-sharp turns and acrobatic aerial dogfighting maneuvers that heavier suits simply couldn't handle.

Though its reduced armor made it more vulnerable to direct heavy attacks, the flight and joint mechanics tested on the Mark XIV laid the foundation for the prehensile, hyper-agile suits that followed, like the Mark XLII. It answered the call during the House Party Protocol before being destroyed in the final "Clean Slate" detonation order.
